From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Arun Iyengar <aiyengar1990@gmail.com>
Date: Tue, 3 Nov 2026 01:15:40 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] media: sunxi: sun50i-di300: add weave, bob, frame-rate and
 TNR modes

The driver only had motion-adaptive deinterlacing with both fields
output. Add the other modes of the vendor driver (BSP 5.4
drivers/char/sunxi-di/drv_div3x, di_client_reset() and
di_dev_apply_fixed_para()) and the temporal noise reduction (TNR)
block, so that every DI feature in the H616 datasheet (section 2.5.2)
can be used:

- V4L2_CID_DEINTERLACING_MODE (driver menu; applications match the
  item names, which are the same in other deinterlacers):
  0 Motion Adaptive, Field Rate: the existing mode, two outputs per
    input frame (vendor "60 Hz" mode);
  1 Motion Adaptive, Frame Rate: one output per input frame, from IN_F1
    and IN_F2 (vendor "30 Hz" mode), written to DIT output 1;
  2 Bob, Frame Rate (default): spatial interpolation of one field, no
    motion detection;
  3 Weave: both fields of the frame put back together unchanged;
  4 Noise Reduction Only: TNR on progressive input, output from the
    TNR write channel (only offered when FUNC_VSN reports TNR);
  5 Bob, Field Rate: both fields interpolated, two outputs per input
    frame, with the field-rate routing of item 0 and all inputs on the
    newest frame (as on the first job of item 0).
  Frame rate outputs one CAPTURE buffer per OUTPUT buffer, field rate
  two, the second timestamped half a frame period after the first: the
  period comes from the previous OUTPUT buffer, or for the first frame
  from the next one if it is already queued; otherwise both carry the
  OUTPUT timestamp.
  The number of CAPTURE buffers per job must not change while either
  queue streams, so a change of rate, or to or from item 4, returns
  -EBUSY then. A change of method at the same rate is accepted; the
  next job starts the new method from the state of a new stream (no
  source history, motion flags or TNR references of the old one). The
  motion-adaptive modes keep one (frame rate, TNR-only) or two (field
  rate) source frames; bob and weave none. Held sources are returned
  at STREAMOFF (and close); there is no drain command.

  The default is "Bob, Frame Rate", as in the Rockchip IEP driver. The
  mem2mem streaming tests of v4l2-compliance (1.32.0,
  v4l2-test-buffers.cpp) handle only one CAPTURE buffer per OUTPUT
  buffer with no source held back: captureBufs() does a blocking DQBUF
  on the OUTPUT queue and then exactly one CAPTURE DQBUF per loop, and
  requires every CAPTURE timestamp to equal that of a queued OUTPUT
  buffer; testRequests() expects every request complete, while the
  request of a held source completes only when the source is released.
  The motion-adaptive and field-rate items therefore cannot be the
  default of a compliance run; they are opt-in.

- Temporal noise reduction (V4L2_CID_SUNXI_DI300_TNR_MODE: off, fixed,
  adaptive; TNR_STRENGTH for the fixed strength, vendor default 0x3a;
  TNR_LEVEL for the adaptive bounds). The vendor's fixed TNR tuning is
  written at resume. In the deinterlacing modes the filtered newest
  frame goes to one of three driver buffers and the filtered previous
  frames replace the original ones as IN_F1/IN_F0 references, as the
  vendor userspace does (recursive filtering); the deinterlaced output
  is then the filtered frame. The adaptive strength follows the
  vendor's di_alg_tnr_strengths_adjustment() from the per-run TNR sums,
  without its scene-change input. The datasheet allows TNR output only
  in YV12 or planar YUV422, and the vendor requires planar DIT output
  with TNR, so TNR is applied only with a planar capture format.

- The capture format may differ from the output format as long as the
  chroma subsampling is the same (the input, DIT and TNR channels have
  separate format fields), e.g. NV12 in and YV12 out as the vendor
  userspace uses. Semi-planar buffers share one UV order bit, so a
  semi-planar capture format keeps the source format.

- Film mode detection: enable the video-on-film detection and flip its
  row-statistics buffer on every run, as the vendor does in field-rate
  mode (the FIELD_HIST statistics come from it). The field-weave
  control elements gain two flags: bit 2 keeps the video blend in
  video-on-film areas (vendor video_exist), bit 3 also weaves chroma.
  Values 0-3 keep their meaning.

- Progressive (V4L2_FIELD_NONE) input is accepted. It is passed
  through (weave, one output per input) in every mode but TNR-only,
  which filters it.

- Buffer metadata as v4l2-compliance expects it of a deinterlacer:
  CAPTURE buffers are V4L2_FIELD_NONE (v4l2_m2m_buf_copy_metadata()
  copied the source field), both queues number their buffers from
  STREAMON, and the payload of an OUTPUT buffer is the one userspace
  queued.

- The driver-private controls (the FMD ones and the new TNR ones) get a
  reserved range, V4L2_CID_USER_SUNXI_DI300_BASE at
  V4L2_CID_USER_BASE + 0x1260 (16 controls; 0x1240 and 0x1250 are taken
  in newer kernels), and a uAPI header, include/uapi/linux/sunxi-di300.h.
  They were at V4L2_CID_USER_BASE + 0x1100, inside the range reserved
  for the MIPI CCS driver.

Assisted-by: LLM
Signed-off-by: Arun Iyengar <aiyengar1990@gmail.com>
